#N canvas 100 100 700 560 10;
#X obj 40 40 jet_win;
#X msg 40 80 create;
#X msg 130 80 destroy;
#X obj 40 130 jet_head 0;
#X obj 40 165 jet_depth 1;
#X obj 40 200 jet_color 1 0.3 0.3;
#X obj 40 235 jet_rectangle 3 2;
#X obj 40 270 jet_color 0.3 0.6 1;
#X obj 40 305 jet_triangle 2;
#X floatatom 160 165 5 0 1 0 - - -;
#X text 210 165 <- depth test on (1) or off (0);
#X text 210 235 red rectangle;
#X text 210 305 blue triangle in the same plane;
#X text 40 350 [jet_depth 1] switches depth testing on (the default \, as in Gem) or off for the shapes after it. With depth testing on \, shapes hide what lies behind them - a rectangle moved back in Z (jet_translateXYZ) disappears behind a cube in front of it. Two shapes in exactly the same plane \, like the ones here \, then compete for the same depth and can flicker against each other. With depth testing off they simply paint over each other in the order the chain draws them (here: the blue triangle always on top).;
#X text 40 480 Left inlet: the chain (bang). Right inlet: the on/off value - it only stores \, the chain's next bang applies it. Chain-scoped: every chain starts with depth on \, and jet_separator restores it after a branch.;
#X connect 1 0 0 0;
#X connect 2 0 0 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 9 0 4 1;
